  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-optgroup-label uses the first child if it's a `legend` element, so placing e.g. a `script` element before it breaks the label. (It's not allowed in the content model, but that could maybe be relaxed in the future to allow intermixing script-supported elements like most other elements.)\n\nI think it would be more robust (and consistent with `fieldset`) to find the first child that is a `legend` element. Was there a reason to be stricter here?\n\n@josepharhar ",
